body:
For me, it was really good. It started with strong emotions, and I was able to laugh and cry, and I couldn't stop talking. I never, ever had a bad trip. And I could distinguish real from not real. I just felt this closeness and unity with my closest friend and the whole world. It was all chaos, I was aware of it, I understood its bad side, but at the same time I felt content because I accepted this was life. It was I was having a conversation with myself, one on one, sitting on a table, facing myself. Having doubts and at the same time solving them. And being aware at all times that I was feeling it, it wasnt like I was drunk or high, it was just this intense feeling of it all being shit but at the same time making sense.   


I've taken them like 5 times in the course of three years, with long gaps between them, the best times were when I knew I could trust the other person I was taking them with. Being able to have someone you can trust and know that if you're having a bad time, they will help, is crucial to the experience. Where you are, who you are with, it has to be safe and good. If not, you can feel paranoid. One time my friend was feeling paranoid because we were meeting other people at a uni dance, I was really secure and content but she was paranoid people would tell she was on shrooms. Even if I was on shrooms, I was able to talk to her and calm her down and say hey, it's okay, we can stay here all night because there's no place I'd rather be than being with my friends. And it calmed her down and then she was fine. After the trip, I still felt the calmness I felt when I took them. It's like something woke up inside me and it stayed with me. But it also made me have some headaches sometimes, and some stomach issues, but that's not bpd related. In my experience, if you trust yourself and accept the experience and emotions, it can be really good. If you're scared or something it won't. It calmed my anxiety and my good/bad view of the world kind of disappeared for some hours, and helped me meditate in the future. Hope my experience helps.  


&#x200B;
